  "about": "I majored in Computer Engineering at Purdue University. I performed a 5-session Co-op with Lutron Electronics, graduating with 18 months of work experience in embedded programming.  After graduating, I worked for Nokia for 5 years in their 'Small-Cells' division as a firmware engineer.  There was a clear need for a Continuous Integration and Deployment and I was a key part in creating their CI/CD process.  I moved to Indiana to be closer to family and took a role on the CI/CD team at Aptiv.  I am currently working at Aptiv as the impromptu Technical Lead for the CI/CD team, where I have been for 5 years.\n\nI have the most experience in Jenkins pipeline scripting (Groovy), Python, and C/C++.  I have used the tools JIRA, Coverity, Confluence, Various C compilers and build systems, and Git/SVN/Plastic SCM on a daily basis for the entirety of my 10-year career.  I am comfortable (and prefer) working in Linux.\n\nI have been a key driver in several Jenkins hosting migrations, build system conversions (Make->CMake and an in-house build system to Bazel), and switched cloud builds from Windows to Linux for significantly reduced build time and server costs.\n\nI am currently looking for a new role related to Embedded development, and even if your role doesn't exactly line up with my experience, I'm always looking for new skills to learn and new ways to grow personally and professionally.",
